15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a heatmap of differentially expressed proteins among three groups labeled Con \(green\), CRKP \(peach\), and KP \(light blue\), with intensity color ranging from blue \(downregulated\) to red \(upregulated\). Panels B, C, and D display volcano plots showing the distribution of protein expression changes by log2 fold-change and statistical significance, highlighting upregulated and downregulated proteins for each group comparison. Panel E presents a KEGG pathway enrichment dot plot, with dot size representing the number of proteins and color indicating statistical significance for biological pathways. Panel F contains a protein interaction network with nodes colored by log2 fold-change, distinguishing upregulated and downregulated proteins.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Nine-panel scientific figure containing three rows labeled A-C, D-F, and G-I. Panels A, D, and G display line graphs of binomial deviance versus log lambda with red trendlines and shaded confidence intervals. Panels B, E, and H show line plots of protein coefficients versus log lambda, each with multiple colored lines. Panels C, F, and I present heatmaps with protein names and variable names along axes, showing correlation values from negative to positive, indicated by a blue to red color scale.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a bar chart comparing AUC and accuracy for three classifiers\204Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost\204on training and testing data. Panel B contains a receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve with AUC values for training and test datasets. Panel C presents a confusion matrix with predicted versus actual values, displaying counts for model predictions. Panel D replicates the bar chart format for a different dataset or outcome. Panel E provides a separate ROC curve with associated AUC metrics. Panel F displays another confusion matrix with distinct prediction results. Panel G features a third bar chart comparison across the same classifiers. Panel H shows a third ROC curve with training and test curve lines. Panel I presents the final confusion matrix summarizing model prediction counts for another classification scenario.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays five gene expression clusters \(Cluster 1 to Cluster 5\), each with membership line plots and expression heatmaps across three conditions \(Con, KP, CRKF\). Statistical enrichment terms and pathways are color-coded by category on the right. Panel B shows a heatmap of correlation coefficients for clinical variables and gene signatures, with a gradient scale from -1 to 1, where color intensity reflects correlation strength and direction.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a bubble plot of GO enrichment for gene ratios, with bubble color and size indicating -log10\(p-value\) and gene number respectively; panel B displays a similar KEGG enrichment plot; panel C shows DO enrichment; panel D is a network diagram showing gene-pathway interactions; panel E is a bar chart of gene counts by category; panel F depicts gene counts by pathway, grouped into Environmental Information Processing, Human Diseases, and Organismal Systems; panel G consists of a hierarchical cluster dendrogram and horizontal bar plot of gene counts across tissues and organ systems; panel H is a circular chord diagram mapping gene status to detection contexts.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a clustered heatmap of metabolite abundance with color-coded groups across samples; Panel B presents a 2D principal component analysis plot showing group clustering; Panel C displays a supervised OPLS-DA scores plot illustrating separation between groups; Panels D, E, and F are volcano plots depicting statistically significant metabolites by fold change and p-value between group comparisons; Panel G is a bubble chart showing metabolic pathway enrichment, with dot size and color indicating significance and pathway impact.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
